    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0430" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 (E.W.)/11–742: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers (Cole) to the War Department
                    </hi><anchor n="41" xml:id="d420-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-04">November 4, 1942</date>.]<lb/>[Received November 5—4
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>No. 757. [From Murphy.] Your M–20, 27th, paragraph 3. In view of message received
                    this morning from Kingpin regarding his decision to proceed North Africa I am
                    informing Flagpole this afternoon on assault date and name of
                    commander-in-chief. To avoid error please confirm assault date. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cole</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d420-f1" n="41" type="source" xml:id="d420-f1-content">
                <p>Copy supplied by the Office of the Secretary of Defense under cover of letter of
                    September 7, 1960.</p>
            </note>
